From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:44:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio: uml: use a 64-bit DMA mask for vhost-user transports

Vhost-user transports guest physical addresses as 64-bit values and maps the complete UML memory table in the userspace backend. The default platform-device mask is only 32 bits, which rejects valid virtio-gpu backing pages once memory pressure moves them above 4 GiB.
---
 arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c b/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
index 18a66122189fb54d8726bb1f28c2830f4e7da743..7b1c3c69b5c396c1def9c8f703dab0d569237138 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/virtio_uml.c
@@ -1233,6 +1233,16 @@ static int virtio_uml_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!vu_dev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * Vhost-user transports guest physical addresses as 64-bit values and
+	 * maps the complete UML memory table in the userspace backend.  The
+	 * default platform-device mask is only 32 bits, which rejects valid
+	 * virtio-gpu backing pages once memory pressure moves them above 4 GiB.
+	 */
+	rc = dma_coerce_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+	if (rc)
+		goto error_free;
+
 	vu_dev->pdata = pdata;
 	vu_dev->vdev.dev.parent = &pdev->dev;
 	vu_dev->vdev.dev.release = virtio_uml_release_dev;
